================================================================================
## MCP client reference implementation and optimization guide (PR #193)
================================================================================

Context:
A generic MCP client for Databricks-hosted OntoBricks deployments, a benchmark
harness, and an optimization guide. Five client-side optimizations (curated tool
descriptions, domain pre-selection, GraphQL schema pre-load, per-tool result
caps, entity-block summarization) cut average latency by 51% and prompt tokens
by 52% on Databricks Claude Haiku 4.5. One Databricks OAuth token serves both the
MCP server and the LLM endpoint. Review fixups by benoitcayladbx are included.

Changes:
1. examples/mcp_client.py (new)
   Reference MCP client (httpx only) with the five optimizations, each
   switchable for comparison; strips extended-thinking `reasoning` blocks
   before echoing assistant messages.
   Review fixups: description for the `run_entity_business_rule` tool (the
   server exposes 14 tools); MCP initialize failures print a stderr warning
   instead of being swallowed.
2. examples/mcp_bench.py (new)
   Benchmark harness: per-question, per-round and per-tool timing plus token
   counts, baseline vs optimized. Review fixup: initialize failures warn on
   stderr.
3. docs/mcp.md
   New "Client Optimization" section (problem, fix, code and measured gain for
   each optimization, plus a which-to-apply table); TOC regenerated. Folded in
   from the proposed standalone docs/mcp-client-optimization.md to follow the
   one-guide-per-category docs layout. Examples anonymized to a neutral sales
   domain (no customer domain or company names in this public repo).

Modified files:
- examples/mcp_client.py (new)
- examples/mcp_bench.py (new)
- docs/mcp.md
- changelogs/v0.9.0/LaurentPRAT-DB_2026-10-11.log (new)

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 8939 passed, 326 skipped,
6 deselected, 1 xfailed (pre-existing), 40 warnings in 116.46s. Both example
scripts compile; docs TOC check passes.
